    <bpmn:process id="W_W2595" name="W2595. Shared Services Technology Investment ROI Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Post-implementation review of shared service automation
Frequency: Post-implementation; quarterly review
Volume: 5–10 active automation projects
Owner: IT Finance Analyst
Participants: IT Finance Analyst, CIO, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W2595 — Shared Services Technology Investment ROI Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W2595_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W2595_Lane1" name="IT Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2595_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2595_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2595_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W2595_Lane2" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2595_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2595_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W2595_Start4" name="Post-implementation review of shared service automation">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2595_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2595_Task5" name="IT Finance Analyst tracks shared service automation project ROI: compares…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IT Finance Analyst tracks shared service automation project ROI: compares projected vs. actual cost savings (AP automation: 30% cost reduction target, payroll automation: 20% error reduction), measures adoption rates and usage metrics, calculates payback period vs. business case
Responsible (R): IT Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CIO / Finance Controller
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2595_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2595_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2595_Task6" name="Analyst identifies underperforming investments: projects not delivering…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Analyst identifies underperforming investments: projects not delivering projected savings, low adoption requiring change management intervention, scope creep increasing cost beyond business case; recommends corrective actions
Responsible (R): IT Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2595_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2595_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2595_Task7" name="Finance Controller incorporates automation savings into shared services cost…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Finance Controller incorporates automation savings into shared services cost budget: adjusts allocation rates downward for functions with realized savings, reallocates saved capacity to growth activities, updates 3-year cost forecast
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2595_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2595_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W2595_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W2595_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W2595_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-447 (ensure controlled execution — Shared Services Performance &amp; Analytics (PA-72.3).) | - operational: capex-approval for automation investment; CTL-637 (technology value realization — realized savings finance-validated and allocation rate adjusted); operational: CIO + Finance Controller quarterly ROI sign-off
Owner: IT Finance Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
